00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:03.540
He's been getting practically straight A's.

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:05.780
You guys talking about Wally?

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:08.260
Oh, never mind, B, but run along, son.

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:09.170
Okay.

00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:13.440
Hey, you know what happened on the way home from school?

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:17.410
Well, I saw Margie and Wally walking together,

00:22:17.510 --> 00:22:19.830
and he had a real nutty smile on his face.

00:22:20.370 --> 00:22:21.150
Yes, dear.

00:22:21.390 --> 00:22:22.550
And then you know what happened?

00:22:22.650 --> 00:22:25.890
He bumped right into a tree, and the smile didn't even go away.

00:22:27.270 --> 00:22:29.590
Beaver, your father and I have something to discuss.

00:22:31.140 --> 00:22:31.760
Yes, Mom.

00:22:33.830 --> 00:22:34.690
You know something, Mom?

00:22:35.340 --> 00:22:35.980
Yes, Beaver.

00:22:37.030 --> 00:22:40.210
Things sure are a lot quieter around here when you did your own housework.

00:22:40.870 --> 00:22:41.510
Beaver.

00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:43.340
Yes, sir.

00:22:46.500 --> 00:22:47.060
Well...

00:22:47.980 --> 00:22:51.020
If Wally's housework is beginning to interfere with his schoolwork,

00:22:51.120 --> 00:22:52.340
I think I'd better have a talk with him.

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:55.460
I just hate to embarrass him, though, about the girl.

00:22:55.910 --> 00:22:57.390
Well, dear, maybe there's another way.

00:22:57.930 --> 00:22:59.870
Why don't you let me have a talk with Mrs. Manners?

00:23:00.820 --> 00:23:01.640
Yeah, that's a good idea.

00:23:02.070 --> 00:23:05.070
After all, it's a lot her fault for having such an attractive daughter.

00:23:08.220 --> 00:23:08.320
Thank you.

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:09.040
Thank you.

00:23:12.630 --> 00:23:13.110
Oh, hi, ma.

00:23:14.810 --> 00:23:17.150
Well, Wally, aren't you home earlier than usual?

00:23:18.010 --> 00:23:18.910
Well, yeah, a little bit.

00:23:19.220 --> 00:23:22.580
But last night I heard you tell Margie that you wanted the kitchen floor waxed.

00:23:22.900 --> 00:23:23.940
So I thought I'd help out.

00:23:24.250 --> 00:23:28.030
Yes, well fine Wally, you go ahead, your assistant's waiting.

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:29.960
Oh, okay, thanks.

00:23:30.020 --> 00:23:30.260
Thanks, Mom.

00:23:33.130 --> 00:23:33.650
Thank you.

00:23:41.930 --> 00:23:42.110
Oh.

00:23:42.600 --> 00:23:43.540
Hello, Mrs. Manners.

00:23:43.960 --> 00:23:45.180
How are you, Wally?

00:23:47.240 --> 00:23:47.520
Okay.

00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:50.780
I must say you're a dear boy to come and help me like this.

00:23:52.300 --> 00:23:53.520
You can start right there.

00:23:54.440 --> 00:23:54.800
Sure.

00:23:56.300 --> 00:23:56.620
Thank you.

00:24:06.390 --> 00:24:08.490
that sort mom and dad for getting rid of Margie

00:24:08.490 --> 00:24:09.730
and getting Mrs. Manners back?

00:24:11.380 --> 00:24:11.740
Well.

00:24:12.150 --> 00:24:13.070
I wasn't first.

00:24:14.840 --> 00:24:15.680
But I've been thinking.

00:24:16.470 --> 00:24:16.990
